<title>USA: GM has 4,250 U.S. workers idled by strike.</title>
<headline>GM has 4,250 U.S. workers idled by strike.</headline>
<dateline>WARREN, Mich. 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp said on Monday that 4,250 of its U.S. employees were laid off as a result of the Canadian Auto Workers strike.  </p>
<p>GM said the strike has affected 1,350 U.S. assembly workers at its Detroit-based Hamtrack assembly plant, which builds Cadillacs.</p>
<p>The strike also has affected total of 2,900 GM powertrain workers at Tonawanda, N.Y., Ypsilanti, Mich. and Flint, Mich.</p>
<p>The strike in Canada began on October 3.</p>
<p>GM said it would not speculate on when or which plants could be affected by the strike.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
